Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• countries.country_name: locate “France” to retrieve its country_id and for later joins with currency  
• countries.country_id: join key between countries and customers to tag each customer with their country  
• customers.cust_id: join key to sales so that only sales whose buyer lives in France are kept  
• customers.country_id: filter customers that belong to France’s country_id  
• promotions.promo_id: join key to sales so we can keep only the rows related to the needed promotions  
• promotions.promo_total_id: must equal 1 (condition) – identifies promotions to include  
• channels.channel_id: join key to sales so we can keep only the rows related to the needed channels  
• channels.channel_total_id: must equal 1 (condition) – identifies channels to include  
• sales.time_id: join key to the times dimension in order to get year & month information  
• sales.amount_sold: base measure to be aggregated, compared and projected  
• times.calendar_year / times.calendar_month_number: filter years 2019, 2020, compute growth and project the same month in 2021  
• products.prod_id: needed to compute growth rate “per product & month”  
• currency.to_us: 2021 exchange rate to convert projected 2021 sales to USD. Join on currency.country = 'France', year = 2021 and month = times.calendar_month_number  

Main conditions that will repeatedly appear  
• promotions.promo_total_id = 1  
• channels.channel_total_id  = 1  
• countries.country_name    = 'France'  
• times.calendar_year IN (2019, 2020)  (when building growth) or = 2021 (when applying growth)  

Below are ten exploratory SQLite queries (LIMIT 20) that progress from simple look‑ups to more complex joins, helping you make sure the required data exists before building the final projection.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Get the country_id value that corresponds to France
SELECT DISTINCT country_id, country_iso_code, country_name
FROM countries
WHERE country_name = 'France'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Verify that customers really exist for France (show 20 of them)
SELECT DISTINCT cust_id, country_id
FROM customers
WHERE country_id = (
      SELECT country_id FROM countries WHERE country_name = 'France'
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: List all channels whose channel_total_id = 1 (these are the channels to keep)
SELECT DISTINCT channel_id, channel_desc, channel_total_id
FROM channels
WHERE channel_total_id = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: List all promotions whose promo_total_id = 1 (these are the promotions to keep)
SELECT DISTINCT promo_id, promo_name, promo_total_id
FROM promotions
WHERE promo_total_id = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Check which calendar years exist in the time dimension
SELECT DISTINCT calendar_year
FROM times
ORDER BY calendar_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Sample raw sales rows for France after joining with customers/countries
SELECT s.prod_id, s.cust_id, s.time_id, s.amount_sold
FROM   sales     AS s
JOIN   customers AS c ON c.cust_id   = s.cust_id
JOIN   countries AS co ON co.country_id = c.country_id
WHERE  co.country_name = 'France'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Sample sales rows that satisfy ALL required filters (France + promo_total_id=1 + channel_total_id=1)
SELECT s.prod_id,
       s.cust_id,
       s.time_id,
       s.amount_sold,
       p.promo_id,
       ch.channel_id
FROM   sales       AS s
JOIN   promotions  AS p  ON p.promo_id  = s.promo_id   AND p.promo_total_id   = 1
JOIN   channels    AS ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
JOIN   customers   AS c  ON c.cust_id   = s.cust_id
JOIN   countries   AS co ON co.country_id = c.country_id
WHERE  co.country_name = 'France'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Aggregate 2019 and 2020 monthly sales per product for France (needed for growth calculation)
SELECT t.calendar_year,
       t.calendar_month_number AS month,
       s.prod_id,
       SUM(s.amount_sold)      AS total_amount
FROM   sales      AS s
JOIN   promotions AS p  ON p.promo_id  = s.promo_id   AND p.promo_total_id   = 1
JOIN   channels   AS ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
JOIN   customers  AS c  ON c.cust_id   = s.cust_id
JOIN   countries  AS co ON co.country_id = c.country_id
JOIN   times      AS t  ON t.time_id   = s.time_id
WHERE  co.country_name = 'France'
  AND  t.calendar_year IN (2019, 2020)
GROUP BY t.calendar_year, t.calendar_month_number, s.prod_id
ORDER BY t.calendar_year, month, s.prod_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Compute growth rate from 2019 to 2020 for each product & month (sample rows)
WITH sales_by_year AS (
    SELECT t.calendar_year  AS yr,
           t.calendar_month_number AS mon,
           s.prod_id              AS prod,
           SUM(s.amount_sold)     AS amt
    FROM   sales      AS s
    JOIN   promotions AS p  ON p.promo_id  = s.promo_id   AND p.promo_total_id   = 1
    JOIN   channels   AS ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
    JOIN   customers  AS c  ON c.cust_id   = s.cust_id
    JOIN   countries  AS co ON co.country_id = c.country_id
    JOIN   times      AS t  ON t.time_id   = s.time_id
    WHERE  co.country_name = 'France'
      AND  t.calendar_year IN (2019, 2020)
    GROUP BY yr, mon, prod
)
SELECT a.mon,
       a.prod,
       a.amt AS amt_2019,
       b.amt AS amt_2020,
       CASE WHEN a.amt > 0 THEN (b.amt - a.amt) * 1.0 / a.amt ELSE NULL END AS growth_rate
FROM   sales_by_year AS a
JOIN   sales_by_year AS b
       ON a.prod = b.prod
      AND a.mon  = b.mon
      AND a.yr   = 2019
      AND b.yr   = 2020
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Project 2021 monthly USD sales using 2019→2020 growth and convert with 2021 FX rate (sample rows)
WITH sales_by_year AS (
    SELECT t.calendar_year  AS yr,
           t.calendar_month_number AS mon,
           s.prod_id              AS prod,
           SUM(s.amount_sold)     AS amt
    FROM   sales      AS s
    JOIN   promotions AS p  ON p.promo_id  = s.promo_id   AND p.promo_total_id   = 1
    JOIN   channels   AS ch ON ch.channel_id = s.channel_id AND ch.channel_total_id = 1
    JOIN   customers  AS c  ON c.cust_id   = s.cust_id
    JOIN   countries  AS co ON co.country_id = c.country_id
    JOIN   times      AS t  ON t.time_id   = s.time_id
    WHERE  co.country_name = 'France'
      AND  t.calendar_year IN (2019, 2020)
    GROUP BY yr, mon, prod
),
growth AS (
    SELECT a.mon,
           a.prod,
           a.amt AS amt_2019,
           b.amt AS amt_2020,
           CASE WHEN a.amt > 0 THEN (b.amt - a.amt) * 1.0 / a.amt ELSE NULL END AS growth_rate
    FROM   sales_by_year AS a
    JOIN   sales_by_year AS b
          ON a.prod = b.prod AND a.mon = b.mon
    WHERE a.yr = 2019 AND b.yr = 2020
),
proj_2021 AS (
    SELECT g.mon,
           g.prod,
           g.amt_2020 * (1 + COALESCE(g.growth_rate,0)) AS projected_amt_2021_local
    FROM   growth AS g
),
fx_2021 AS (
    SELECT month, to_us
    FROM   currency
    WHERE  country = 'France' AND year = 2021
)
SELECT p.mon,
       ROUND(AVG(p.projected_amt_2021_local / f.to_us), 2) AS avg_projected_sales_usd
FROM   proj_2021 AS p
JOIN   fx_2021   AS f ON f.month = p.mon
GROUP BY p.mon
ORDER BY p.mon
LIMIT 20;
```
